    ],
    "text": "The Great Lakes, holding 21% of the world's fresh surface water, face complex water level management challenges due to natural and human factors. This study presents an Adaptive Hydrological Network Simulation and an Equilibrium Stake- holder Satisfaction (ESS) Model to address these challenges. The network model represents the lakes as interconnected nodes and edges, simplifying the system's complexity and facilitating analysis. The ESS Model integrates stakeholder prefer- ences, prioritizing their diverse interests in water level management."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000013",
    "issues": [
